<p>Follow these steps to load a printing preferences settings file as a one 
 click preset. This file would be provided by an administrator, for example.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span> on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab. The <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Import...</span>. 
 The <span class="Term-OS">Open</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the file containing the printing preferences settings, 
 and then click <span class="Term-OS">Open</span>.<br/>
 The printing preferences settings file is loaded and the one click preset 
 is registered.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
